  "slug": "mechanism-activation-0dd2",
  "summary": "Enhanced-sampling and ML analyses of class A GPCRs now test hybrid and allosteric activation models at atomic resolution.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is conformational control of GPCR activation, approached through simulation and data-driven analysis of structures rather than new experimental determinations. A machine learning framework applied to experimental class A GPCR structures proposes a hybrid activation model in which ligand binding follows conformational selection, and the study also addresses G protein binding. For the plant receptor GCR1, MD and metadynamics simulations propose that abscisic acid binding closes GPA1, trapping GDP and blocking nucleotide exchange. For GLP-1R, enhanced-sampling simulations characterize how an ago-allosteric modulator stabilizes active conformations and identify two intermediate activation states. What is new is the explicit atomistic description of intermediate states and allosteric coupling to G protein signaling across receptor systems, although these results remain computational predictions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-03-27"
